    "body": "A head-turning statistic surrounding the availability, or rather lack thereof, of Barcelona star Andreas Christensen during his time with the club has come to the fore online. This comes fresh off the Dane suffering yet another fitness setback late this week. After spending the duration of the international break in Catalunya’s capital working to secure a return to peak fitness, stopper Christensen was forced to sit out training on Friday. As per an ensuing statement released by Barcelona: ‘First team player Andreas Christensen has slight discomfort in his left calf. He is doubtful for the next game. His recovery time will depend on how the discomfort develops.’ MEDICAL NEWS First team player Andreas Christensen has slight discomfort in his left calf. He is doubtful for the next game. His recovery time will depend on how the discomfort develops. pic.twitter.com/DXEKeBPuyC Such struggles are hardly a new development for Christensen at Barcelona, with the former Chelsea man having struggled with injuries throughout his time at the Camp Nou. So much so that they have this week given rise to a head-turning statistic. As revealed by Diario Sport : ‘Since arriving in the summer of 2017, the Danish defender has missed exactly 100 matches with Barça due to injury and has played 106.’ Conor Laird – GSFN",
